====== TP-Link RE650 v1======

{{page>meta:infobox:construction&noheader&nofooter&noeditbtn}}

{{:media:tplink:re650_image.jpg?400|}}

The TP-Link RE650 is a dual-band 4×4 MIMO 802.11a/n/ac (5GHz)/4×4 MIMO 802.11b/g/n (2.4GHz) "range extender" with a single Gigabit Ethernet port, powered by an internal power supply. As usual with range extenders the whole unit is designed to be plugged directly into a wall outlet.

===== Supported Versions =====

The TP-Link RE650 has been produced in two revisions, "1.0" and "2.0" (labeled "v1" and "v2" by OpenWrt). The revisions are easily distinguishable by the label on the device: it states "1.0" or "2.0" next to the region code. Hardware-wise the revisions are largely identical, the main difference being the v2 revision only offering half of the flash memory (8 MB vs. 16 MB).

For now, this TOH page only deals with the v1 revision, [[toh:tp-link:re650_v2|the v2 revision has its own TOH page]].

