==== Installation via OEM web interface ====

  * set your PC to a static IP in the 192.168.0.x range (e.g. 192.168.0.2)
  * connect your PC to the ethernet port on the side of the unit
  * open the web interface at http://192.168.0.254/
  * navigate the web interface to Settings > System Tools > Firmware Upgrade
  * for good measure, compare the revision (i.e., "1.0" for v1) is shown as "Hardware Version"
  * upload the OpenWrt ''factory.bin'' image and confirm

The flashing process takes about 90 seconds, the first boot of OpenWrt will take a minute, subsequent boots are much faster. You can now reset your PC's IP address to DHCP or a static 192.168.1.x address and, as is common, access OpenWrt on the device at ''192.168.1.1''.
